  "worked_solution": "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{4x-3}-\\frac{3}{8x-6} & =\\frac{9}{4x-3}-\\frac{3}{2(4x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9(2)-3}{2(4x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2(4x-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n2(4x-3)=0\\,\u27f9\\,x=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptote is at $x=\\frac{3}{4}.$",
